00:23:20.811 --> 00:23:23.275
processes which are a really
nice way of formalizing,

00:23:23.276 --> 00:23:28.540
selecting sort of diverse sets
of points or features,

00:23:28.541 --> 00:23:30.090
there's classification
based methods

00:23:30.091 --> 00:23:31.060
where you sort of run

00:23:31.061 --> 00:23:32.730
classification
using small subsets

00:23:32.731 --> 00:23:33.915
of the features, and use this.

00:23:33.916 --> 00:23:35.805
So there's lots of things
have been studied here.

00:23:35.806 --> 00:23:37.570
For example with this problem,
the solution really

00:23:37.571 --> 00:23:39.975
when in this case as usual
want to be super hard,

00:23:39.976 --> 00:23:41.735
I could cluster my data first,

00:23:41.736 --> 00:23:44.600
I could explicitly identify
these clusters, and then,

00:23:44.601 --> 00:23:46.020
I could re-balance
my sampling to

00:23:46.021 --> 00:23:47.520
try to get enough points
