00:24:23.511 --> 00:24:26.350
So, in a sense they're sort
of inherently heuristic,

00:24:26.351 --> 00:24:27.805
or ad hoc because we don't have,

00:24:27.806 --> 00:24:29.170
before we have a good definition

00:24:29.171 --> 00:24:32.480
of what a good sampling is.

00:24:32.481 --> 00:24:37.570
Okay. So that's sort of
the goal of my work on sampling,

00:24:37.571 --> 00:24:39.370
which is basically
to understand what is

00:24:39.371 --> 00:24:41.510
the right way to
select data points,

00:24:41.511 --> 00:24:44.650
or features for generic
linear algebraic computation

00:24:44.651 --> 00:24:47.830
to do fast approximately
algebraic computation.

00:24:47.831 --> 00:24:50.970
This is obviously
an interesting question for

00:24:50.971 --> 00:24:53.970
all sorts of algorithms and
learning, in optimization.

00:24:53.971 --> 00:24:56.220
I'm focusing specifically
here on linear and algebra.

00:24:56.221 --> 00:24:58.145
I want some generic
sampling method

00:24:58.146 --> 00:25:00.140
that lets me speed
up like solving

00:25:00.141 --> 00:25:02.100
linear systems linear
approximation and a lot of

00:25:02.101 --> 00:25:05.670
the standards of
those computational tools.

00:25:05.671 --> 00:25:08.120
So the first step is that

00:25:08.121 --> 00:25:09.960
in designing such a
sampling scheme is

00:25:09.961 --> 00:25:13.345
we're going to restrict the
types of schemes we consider.

00:25:13.346 --> 00:25:15.550
Specifically, we're going
only look at schemes

00:25:15.551 --> 00:25:18.045
which are relatively
simple random processes.

00:25:18.046 --> 00:25:19.460
I'm only going to
look at sampling

00:25:19.461 --> 00:25:20.975
schemes that look like this.

00:25:20.976 --> 00:25:23.090
I assign some sort of score,

00:25:23.091 --> 00:25:24.770
some probability between zero

00:25:24.771 --> 00:25:26.710
and one for every row
in my matrix.

00:25:26.711 --> 00:25:28.620
This represents
the sort of importance

00:25:28.621 --> 00:25:30.360
of that point in
composing my matrix,

00:25:30.361 --> 00:25:31.820
or my dataset, which I'll

00:25:31.821 --> 00:25:33.800
explain how we
compute these later.

00:25:33.801 --> 00:25:35.670
And then what I do
is for every point,

00:25:35.671 --> 00:25:37.200
I just sample independently

00:25:37.201 --> 00:25:39.630
at random with probability Pi.

00:25:39.631 --> 00:25:41.960
And so it means
that one time have

00:25:41.961 --> 00:25:43.630
this important sampling
distribution set,

00:25:43.631 --> 00:25:45.140
my sampling process
is super easy.

00:25:45.141 --> 00:25:46.950
It's just flipping
a bunch of biased coins,

00:25:46.951 --> 00:25:49.100
in this case is
my sample from my matrix.

00:25:49.101 --> 00:25:50.690
And then, I'm going to
hope that this sample

00:25:50.691 --> 00:25:51.870
somehow well represents

00:25:51.871 --> 00:25:55.910
my original data in some metric.

00:25:55.911 --> 00:25:58.620
And we're going to analyze
the effects of the sampling.

00:25:58.621 --> 00:26:00.600
I'm not going to get into
this at all during this talk,

00:26:00.601 --> 00:26:01.770
but we're going
to analyze this as

00:26:01.771 --> 00:26:03.720
a random process, we'll review,

00:26:03.721 --> 00:26:05.550
selecting these points
as basically

00:26:05.551 --> 00:26:07.220
choosing a random
sampling matrix,

00:26:07.221 --> 00:26:09.120
and applying it to
our matrix where just

00:26:09.121 --> 00:26:11.495
selects out individual rows
of the matrix.

00:26:11.496 --> 00:26:13.620
This is like not, it's not

00:26:13.621 --> 00:26:15.755
a huge technical innovation
or anything like this,

00:26:15.756 --> 00:26:17.590
but doing random sampling

00:26:17.591 --> 00:26:19.835
makes analysis way
easier than for example,

00:26:19.836 --> 00:26:21.820
we could have computed
all the scores,

00:26:21.821 --> 00:26:22.640
and then just selected

00:26:22.641 --> 00:26:23.900
the points with
the highest scores,

00:26:23.901 --> 00:26:25.210
or something like this, but

00:26:25.211 --> 00:26:26.880
these things become really
difficult to analyze.

00:26:26.881 --> 00:26:28.060
Here, we just have
a really simple

00:26:28.061 --> 00:26:29.380
independent sampling process and

00:26:29.381 --> 00:26:33.630
that's how we're going to try
to approximate our matrix.

00:26:33.631 --> 00:26:36.490
So then the question
becomes how do we

00:26:36.491 --> 00:26:38.360
compute these probabilities Pi?

00:26:38.361 --> 00:26:40.545
So, naturally you think,

00:26:40.546 --> 00:26:42.675
well it depends on the problem
I'm trying to solve.

00:26:42.676 --> 00:26:45.035
So, for linear systems,

00:26:45.036 --> 00:26:48.480
I'm trying to solve this problem
minimize Ax minus b.

00:26:48.481 --> 00:26:51.930
What I might want is that
after I sample my matrix,

00:26:51.931 --> 00:26:55.485
so I instead to solve the
problem on- it's not working.

00:26:55.486 --> 00:26:57.630
I instead solve
the problem on SA,

00:26:57.631 --> 00:26:59.390
the sampled version of matrix,

00:26:59.391 --> 00:27:02.065
and Sb, the sampled version
of the output vector.

00:27:02.066 --> 00:27:04.280
I might want this to give me
a reasonably good solution.

00:27:04.281 --> 00:27:07.045
Maybe, it's a near minimum
for my original problem.

00:27:07.046 --> 00:27:08.830
So this is I would try

00:27:08.831 --> 00:27:09.970
to look for sampling
probabilities,

00:27:09.971 --> 00:27:11.080
I guarantee that
this is going to

00:27:11.081 --> 00:27:13.310
happen with good probability.

00:27:13.311 --> 00:27:15.470
For low-rank approximation,

00:27:15.471 --> 00:27:16.790
I might ask a different thing,

00:27:16.791 --> 00:27:19.985
I want to sample my matrix,

00:27:19.986 --> 00:27:22.590
so I have this matrix essay,
my sample matrix,

00:27:22.591 --> 00:27:23.830
I want- it's going to be much

00:27:23.831 --> 00:27:25.180
smaller than my original matrix,

00:27:25.181 --> 00:27:27.585
I want to compute
its top singular vectors,

00:27:27.586 --> 00:27:29.410
and then I want to
project onto them,

00:27:29.411 --> 00:27:33.425
compute this AV,
AVs, Vs transpose.

00:27:33.426 --> 00:27:35.590
This is a low rank
matrix, if I sent.

00:27:35.591 --> 00:27:39.715
If Vs has k columns
this is a k rank matrix.

00:27:39.716 --> 00:27:42.380
I want this to be a near
optimal low-rank approximation

00:27:42.381 --> 00:27:44.815
if I look at
all ranking matrices,

00:27:44.816 --> 00:27:46.130
this one is nearly as close as

00:27:46.131 --> 00:27:47.950
possible to my original matrix.

00:27:47.951 --> 00:27:50.025
So there's a sort of
optimization viewpoint of

00:27:50.026 --> 00:27:53.365
how can I solve this problem
approximately well.

00:27:53.366 --> 00:27:56.040
The problem is, is
that, if we start going

00:27:56.041 --> 00:27:57.960
through all these
various problems,

00:27:57.961 --> 00:27:59.060
it seems like we're
going to require

00:27:59.061 --> 00:28:00.890
a different sampling
distributions in

00:28:00.891 --> 00:28:02.270
a sort of different analysis for

00:28:02.271 --> 00:28:04.400
every single problem that
we're trying to solve.

00:28:04.401 --> 00:28:05.840
And this isn't
what I want. I want

00:28:05.841 --> 00:28:07.090
something that is very general,

00:28:07.091 --> 00:28:09.570
just like you can do
very general analysis

00:28:09.571 --> 00:28:11.145
of things like
stochastic already set.

00:28:11.146 --> 00:28:12.375
I want something
that applies to a

00:28:12.376 --> 00:28:14.000
huge range of problems at once.

00:28:14.001 --> 00:28:15.510
So you can just take
the same problem,

00:28:15.511 --> 00:28:16.880
the same algorithm, and apply it

00:28:16.881 --> 00:28:19.130
to a bunch of
different problems.

00:28:19.131 --> 00:28:23.480
And the key idea here is
also pretty simple but it's

00:28:23.481 --> 00:28:25.230
pretty powerful is
that instead of looking

00:28:25.231 --> 00:28:27.045
at problem specific guarantees,

00:28:27.046 --> 00:28:28.320
or I want to approximate

00:28:28.321 --> 00:28:31.295
this problem like
nearly optimally,

00:28:31.296 --> 00:28:32.870
we're going to look at

00:28:32.871 --> 00:28:35.720
really simple spectral
approximation guarantees.

00:28:35.721 --> 00:28:40.450
What this means is I'm going
to ask for any vector x,

00:28:40.451 --> 00:28:42.920
I'm going to want to preserve
the product with my matrix.

00:28:42.921 --> 00:28:45.375
I'm going to want to preserve
the product A times x.

00:28:45.376 --> 00:28:47.410
So, specifically, if I

00:28:47.411 --> 00:28:49.540
look at the product
with my sample matrix,

00:28:49.541 --> 00:28:51.410
I want this norm to be

00:28:51.411 --> 00:28:52.230
close to the norm of

00:28:52.231 --> 00:28:53.410
the product with
the original matrix.

00:28:53.411 --> 00:28:55.290
